wod.Repelled by garlic and holy symbols: presented with either, a Willpower roll or they must remove themselves from its presence.=Repelled by garlic and holy symbols: presented with either, a Willpower roll or they must remove themselves from its presence.
wod.Given over to their own savagery, they suffer the same frenzy effects as the Brujah.=Given over to their own savagery, they suffer the same frenzy effects as the Brujah.
wod.+2 difficulty on every roll to resist frenzy. They may not spend Willpower to avoid a frenzy, only to end one.=+2 difficulty on every roll to resist frenzy. They may not spend Willpower to avoid a frenzy, only to end one.
wod.Broken by centuries of infernal servitude, they are extraordinarily suggestible: +2 difficulty on all Willpower rolls.=Broken by centuries of infernal servitude, they are extraordinarily suggestible: +2 difficulty on all Willpower rolls.
wod.They take aggravated damage from silver.=They take aggravated damage from silver.
wod.Centuries under the Tremere left them far from their human side: no Ducheski may ever have a Social Attribute above 2.=Centuries under the Tremere left them far from their human side: no Ducheski may ever have a Social Attribute above 2.
wod.Centuries of moral decay: they may not have Humanity higher than 3, nor Conscience higher than 2.=Centuries of moral decay: they may not have Humanity higher than 3, nor Conscience higher than 2.
wod.Tzimisce blood runs thin in this family, which has no native ties to the Voivodate: they have only eight blood points.=Tzimisce blood runs thin in this family, which has no native ties to the Voivodate: they have only eight blood points.
wod.Family arrogance: whenever there is a chance to boast of the family, a Willpower roll at difficulty 7 to hold back their scorn.=Family arrogance: whenever there is a chance to boast of the family, a Willpower roll at difficulty 7 to hold back their scorn.
wod.Years of genetic manipulation: every member suffers the Slow Healing Flaw (V20 p. 483).=Years of genetic manipulation: every member suffers the Slow Healing Flaw (V20 p. 483).
wod.All Keskinen share their patron's obsession with blotting out the sun, which manifests as a Derangement.=All Keskinen share their patron's obsession with blotting out the sun, which manifests as a Derangement.
wod.Vulnerable to sunlight: they take sunlight damage as a Cainite would, but bashing rather than aggravated, and may soak it with Stamina and Fortitude.=Vulnerable to sunlight: they take sunlight damage as a Cainite would, but bashing rather than aggravated, and may soak it with Stamina and Fortitude.
wod.Krevcheski are distrusted by the Tzimisce, and thus have only learned two family Disciplines instead of the normal three.=Krevcheski are distrusted by the Tzimisce, and thus have only learned two family Disciplines instead of the normal three.
wod.Quite susceptible to the blood bond: they become Bound to a vampire after a single drink.=Quite susceptible to the blood bond: they become Bound to a vampire after a single drink.
wod.Bred for intellect and prone to psychological disorders: the vast majority suffer the Obsessive-Compulsive Derangement (V20 pp. 291-292).=Bred for intellect and prone to psychological disorders: the vast majority suffer the Obsessive-Compulsive Derangement (V20 pp. 291-292).
wod.Members of the resurging Narov line are afflicted with the Megalomania Derangement instead (V20 pp. 291-292).=Members of the resurging Narov line are afflicted with the Megalomania Derangement instead (V20 pp. 291-292).
wod.Cursed for their founders' crimes: they suffer the Haunted Flaw (V20 p. 495) permanently, and banishing one ghost only brings another.=Cursed for their founders' crimes: they suffer the Haunted Flaw (V20 p. 495) permanently, and banishing one ghost only brings another.
wod.Cursed by the moon: +2 difficulty to use Disciplines at the new moon, +1 waxing and waning, -1 at the full moon. Their blood rejects the Embrace, which has always killed them.=Cursed by the moon: +2 difficulty to use Disciplines at the new moon, +1 waxing and waning, -1 at the full moon. Their blood rejects the Embrace, which has always killed them.
wod.All of them suffer the Deathsight Flaw (V20 p. 494): -2 difficulty to resist Appearance-based rolls, +2 difficulty on Perception rolls and +1 on Social rolls.=All of them suffer the Deathsight Flaw (V20 p. 494): -2 difficulty to resist Appearance-based rolls, +2 difficulty on Perception rolls and +1 on Social rolls.
wod.In the presence of a vampire descended from Anushin-Rawan they are compelled to protect that Ventrue as if blood bound, for 10 nights minus their Willpower.=In the presence of a vampire descended from Anushin-Rawan they are compelled to protect that Ventrue as if blood bound, for 10 nights minus their Willpower.
wod.Addictive personalities: exposed to a sensual experience that has weakened them, a Willpower roll to do anything but pursue it, and Willpower may not be spent to resist the addiction.=Addictive personalities: exposed to a sensual experience that has weakened them, a Willpower roll to do anything but pursue it, and Willpower may not be spent to resist the addiction.
wod.Every Vlaszy swears a Blood Oath to a Fiend upon reaching the age of majority.=Every Vlaszy swears a Blood Oath to a Fiend upon reaching the age of majority.
wod.Exposed to a pleasurable experience, a Willpower roll or they become obsessed with it. They may not spend Willpower to resist a supernatural power that entices them to a new pleasure.=Exposed to a pleasurable experience, a Willpower roll or they become obsessed with it. They may not spend Willpower to resist a supernatural power that entices them to a new pleasure.
